  "body": "Auction: 34 Shortland Street, City on Wednesday 2 December 2026 at 1:30PM  (unless sold prior)\r\n\r\nPeaceful, private and one of Auckland’s best-kept secrets, Karaka Bay offers a rare coastal lifestyle. Elevated above the secluded beach, this architecturally designed cedar home sits amid established native trees and abundant birdlife on 982m² of freehold land, cherished by its owners for over 30 years.\r\n\r\nSweeping views across the sparkling harbour to Browns Island and Musik Point unfold from each level. Spacious, light-filled living areas open to sunny wraparound decks, while generous bedrooms include a master with an ensuite and private deck. Character-filled gardens reveal delightful hideaways and quiet retreats.\r\n\r\nModernised kitchen and bathrooms, garaging, extensive storage, office or hobbies spaces, workshop and ample parking provide comfortable and practical living, with exciting scope to renovate, reimagine or build your dream home.\r\n\r\nStroll to the beach and waterfront reserves for morning swims, picnics or kayaking. Close to Churchill Park, coastal walkways and St Heliers Village. In zone for Churchill Park School, Glendowie College and handy to Sacred Heart College and St Ignatius schools.\r\n\r\nWith retirement beckoning, the owners reluctantly farewell their much-loved home, offering another family the chance to create decades of memories in this remarkable coastal setting.",
